      "value": {
        "severity": "low",
        "id": "stale-lock-reclaim-toctou",
        "detail": "withDirectoryLock stale reclaim is check-then-act and the finally-rm deletes whatever directory is at the lock path, so two waiters racing a stale lock can both enter the read-modify-write and drop one entry; fails closed via pointer reconciliation (blocking missing:<id> violation) but the emitted detail then wrongly accuses ledger tampering; fix is an atomic rename-based reclaim plus a holder token checked before the finally-rm"
